Item #:  SCP-5127-k

Object Class:  Euclid

Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5127-k is to be kept inside Steve Carell's mansion. There it has a room that the foundation has made into a look-alike Michael Scott's office. To Keep SCP-5127-k busy, It has a number of desk toys that It can interact and play with. Including a Train whistle, a small slinky, a rubric's cube and silly putty. It also can be kept busy with a phone with recorded voices.

Description:  SCP-5127-k is a translucent ghost version of Michael Gary Scott, the branch manager of Dunder Mifflin Scranton SCP-5127-k first appeared when Steve Carell finished The Office in 2011. Before the foundation knew anything about SCP-5127-k, It was roaming Steve Carell's mansion. After Steve Carrel said anything, SCP-5127-k responded with  Recently the foundation has recorded 600,000 USD that Steve Carrel has lost to SCP-5127-k.



